Yes, A CUDA can definitely throw an out-of Memory error when a large array is created. In C, an array of 1 million elements is indeed too large for the standard memory. In C, a C program can only address a maximum of 3 GB of RAM. 

 Here is a simple C code that creates an array of 1000000 elements. 

``` C
#include <stdio.h>

int main()
{
    int a[1000000];
    return 0;
}
```

 When you run this program, the operating system will throw an out-of Memory error.
